Description: A failed effect preview keeps its row and says so
 A preview that fails no longer takes its effect away: upstream removed
 the row in 2D (view.model.remove(index)), and in 3D the grid kept a
 black tile without a word. Now, in 2D and 3D alike, the row stays, the
 tile shows "No preview for this effect" with the effect's name, the
 reason goes to the log once per effect, and the effect can still be
 chosen. PipelineItem's failed() carries GStreamer's reason, and a
 preview that cannot be linked to its sink fails instead of asserting.
 When a chosen effect cannot start in the flat camera (its element is
 missing, or the description is refused), the camera runs without it and
 the viewfinder says so (WebcamControl::effectMessage); before, the
 description was handed to camerabin half-built with only a debug line.
 This is the edition's reading of Daniel Campos Ramos's rules ("nothing
 we do should silently fail", 2026-11-01; "do not remove
 functionality!", 2026-10-08), not upstream's behaviour.
 The two new sentences are translated into the nine languages Kamoso
 ships besides English (de, es, fr, ja, ko, pl, pt_BR, zh_CN, zh_TW); the
 translations are ours.
 configgrid-test: a failed preview keeps its row; a model row whose
 element does not exist keeps its row, shows the sentence, can be chosen
 and is logged once, in 2D and in 3D. The stand-in PipelineItem asks
 GStreamer's own parser, as the real item does.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24

